 "answer_verbatim": "There isn’t one universally “best” title company—it depends on the property, closing timeline, and whether you want an attorney involved. **Marina Title** is one Miami-area option worth comparing: its public listings show strong customer ratings and reviews praising communication and smooth closings, though some reviewers report delays or unexpected fees.\n\nBefore choosing, get written estimates from two or three companies and compare the title search, title insurance, settlement, wire, and remote-closing fees. Ask who will handle your file, how quickly they respond, and whether they can meet your closing date. You can also check the company or agent through the Florida Department of Financial Services and ask your real-estate attorney or lender whether they have any concerns.",
